      "speaker": "narrator",
      "start": 0.15,
      "end": 4.35,
      "text": "Everyone swore light was tiny bullets—until two beams crossed and created darkness."
    },
    {
      "id": "L2",
      "beatId": "B2",
      "speaker": "newton",
      "start": 4.60,
      "end": 6.85,
      "text": "Light travels straight! Mere particles!"
    },
    {
      "id": "L3",
      "beatId": "B2",
      "speaker": "huygens",
      "start": 7.05,
      "end": 9.35,
      "text": "Then watch it bend like ripples, Sir Isaac."
    },
    {
      "id": "L4",
      "beatId": "B3",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "start": 9.60,
      "end": 15.30,
      "text": "In 1678, Christiaan Huygens proved every point on a wavefront sparks fresh baby ripples—forming interference."
    },
    {
      "id": "L5",
      "beatId": "B4",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "start": 15.60,
      "end": 18.25,
      "text": "Inside Iceland spar crystal, one beam splits in two!"
    },
    {
      "id": "L6",
      "beatId": "B4",
      "speaker": "newton",
      "start": 18.45,
      "end": 20.30,
      "text": "Impossible! Bullets don't ripple!"
    },
    {
      "id": "L7",
      "beatId": "B5",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "start": 20.60,
      "end": 25.25,
      "text": "He also built the pendulum clock and unveiled Saturn's rings with wave-honed lenses."
    },
    {
      "id": "L8",
      "beatId": "B6",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "start": 25.60,
      "end": 29.60,
      "text": "Lasers, Wi-Fi, and 5G today? All surfing Huygens' waves."
